          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The form the book owed you longest. (Hablasteis.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two chants, and each is a whole tense."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The preterite. Hablé, hablaste, habló, hablamos, hablasteis, hablaron. Six of six, and the same for -er, for -ir, and for every strong stem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The imperfect. Hablaba, hablabas, hablaba, hablábamos, hablabais, hablaban. Six of six, with exactly three irregular verbs in the whole language — ser, ir, ver — and you hold all of them."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neither of those sentences has a note at the end saying the rest is coming later. That is new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: where the accents fall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The one thing worth keeping separate is the accents, because the two imperfect sets behave in opposite ways."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the -aba set, one form carries a mark: hablábamos, and only because the stress falls where the default would not put it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the -ía set, every form carries one, and for a different reason entirely: the i and the a would otherwise run together into a single beat, and the accent holds them apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
